  "text": "2.2 OK. So today I want to talk about a place with extreme temperatures. Take a look at the photos. What seasons do you see? Summer. Winter. Yes, that's right. Autumn. And... Spring. Yes. And they're all from one place, the central part of Hokkaido, in Japan. It has hot summers and cold winters. Let's look at photo A. What can we see? Well, it's a hot day in summer. And there's a beautiful lake and a beach. There's a blue sky and it's sunny. There are some beautiful lakes in central Hokkaido, so people like to swim and fish. Now here, in photo B, it's winter. There's lots of snow. It's also very cold. The temperature can get to minus 12 degrees Celsius. In photo C, you can see it's autumn. The temperature is a little cold, and the trees change colour to red and orange. There are many trees in Hokkaido, so it's very beautiful. And now we see spring in photo D. After the cold weather, spring is welcome in Hokkaido. The weather is warm, so the flowers grow. As you can see, Hokkaido is a place with four seasons and extreme temperatures in winter. But it's a beautiful place, so people like to do things outside.",
